course: dictionary
lesson: 232
title: Allied and the power of context
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Read the words around the word, and ask what would fit. «On 6 June 1944, D-Day, Allied troops landed on the beaches of Normandy in France.» The capital A and the word troops are clues that Allied means countries fighting together, not just friends.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Swap in joined together with others and read it again: "joined together with others troops landed on the beaches" still makes sense, so you are on the right track. Context clues are often a sentence or two away, so read on before you decide.
explain: Allied is also the past form of the verb ally, which means to join up with someone to help them. So you might see allied as a verb in a sentence about two groups who joined together, or as an adjective describing a group that is already joined together.
fact: Allied means joined together with others to help each other, especially in a war.
fact: The Allies were the countries that fought together against Germany and its partners in the two World Wars.
fact: «Allied troops» are soldiers from the countries fighting on the same side, such as those who landed in Normandy on D-Day.
fact: Allied can also mean connected or related, like allied subjects, or allied health workers such as physiotherapists.
fact: Allied is the past form of the verb ally, so you can say that two groups allied with each other.
exercise: «On 6 June 1944, D-Day, Allied troops landed on the beaches of Normandy in France.» What does Allied mean here? | *Joined together with others, fighting on the same side | Very old and famous | Lost and confused | Painted in bright colours
exercise: In history, the Allies were the countries that fought together against whom? | *Germany and its partners in the two World Wars | Countries that never went to war | Their friends in the local park | Only France in one small battle
exercise: Which of these is a meaning of allied that is NOT about war? | *Connected or related, like allied subjects | Holding a pencil | Painted in the colour blue | Very old
test: What do «Allied forces» mean? | Sleepy sheep in a field | Very tall buildings | *Soldiers and ships of countries fighting together | A shop that sells forks and spoons
test: Ally is a verb. Which sentence uses allied correctly as its past form? | The allied sun was hot in the garden | She is very allied today | I allied a red apple on the table | *The two villages allied to share the cost of the bridge
exam: Which clue in «Allied troops landed on the beaches of Normandy in France» best shows the Allies were a team of countries? | *The word Allied shows many countries acted together as one side | The beaches were sandy | Normandy is in France | The landing was on 6 June
